<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices fall on improved supplies.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices fall on improved supplies.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices fell on Monday on reduced demand from processing plants and better supplies, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices fell by 50-100 rupees per tonne in central Indian markets. Soyoil fell by 200 rupees, reacting to increased sales from soy plants and refineries.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction were slightly down on reduced export enquiries. Soymeal yellow was quoted $280-281 per tonne in export deals. Rapeseed extraction was quoted at $124 per tonne for ready shipment.</p>
